description=A small 1993 Unix on the desktop computers of Knox County. Switch one on, sit down at it, and a green 60x20 terminal opens on a BIOS line and a login prompt. <LINE> <LINE>
description=Files, permissions, accounts, a shell with pipes and cron. The doors, lights, curtains, windows, oven, generator and television of the building under /dev, once you have screwed a module onto them. Coax to the machines next door, a modem to the county, a radio past both. <LINE> <LINE>
description=And a crontab line runs them without you: curtains at dawn and dusk, the set on for its programme, a door that shuts itself, an alarm that names the window somebody opened. <LINE> <LINE>
description=Most computers come up as somebody's: his accounts, his files, a week of his log, and his password written down somewhere in the building. <LINE> <LINE>
description=Server-authoritative and safe in multiplayer. No dependencies. Build 42 only. <LINE> <LINE>
